## Practical redesign arithmetic
- Bare-only exact-output quotient: 77984. Six Pilaster/Ogive IDs require 16 component outputs each; three Trestle IDs require 64. This discards latent role/facing.
- Tailored Atelier: 6 × 16 + 3 × 64 + 126 × 112 = 14400; catalog becomes 59840. The 112-state restriction preserves planner poses, not all arbitrary saves.
- Legacy rectangle planner: 42 poses × 4 facings × 3 stones × 5 cloths = 2520; combined catalog 50840.
- Retain role 5 as well: 50 poses × 60 = 3000; combined catalog 51320.

## Limitations
- Component equivalence is not decoded-state or future editor equivalence.
- Different geometry identifiers are not resolved to mesh equivalence.
- Counts of unique signatures are not automatically realizable Cartesian state declarations; packed domains may require padding or ID splits.
- Planner restriction excludes arbitrary historical role/mask combinations and needs an explicit migration policy.
- No source definitions, worlds, schemas or packages are changed.

## Reproduce
node --experimental-strip-types tools/audit-state-redundancy.mjs "/workspace/scratch/212c580ada5b/altare-editor-review-20261103" "/workspace/scratch/212c580ada5b/altare-two-pillars-integration-20261103/out/two-pedestal-integration"

The JSON contains every audited block and SHA-256 hashes of the package, manifest, source codecs/planner and all input block definitions.
